# Local Windows install

After squash-merging an app change into `main` (frontend, backend, or bundled resources), rebuild and silently reinstall the fork. Do not wait for the user to ask. Skip docs-only PRs.

1. Stop running `FloorPoV` processes.
2. VS 2022 `vcvars64.bat` + bun on PATH.
3. Temp JSON `{"bundle":{"createUpdaterArtifacts":false}}`, then `bun x tauri build --ci --config <file>`. Never extra `--` before `--ci`.
4. Install `FloorPoV_*_x64-setup.exe /S` over `%LOCALAPPDATA%\FloorPoV\FloorPoV.exe`.
5. Copy the setup to `%USERPROFILE%\Downloads` and relaunch. Keep auto-update off.

If signing fails but the NSIS file exists, install it anyway.
